{"title": "Announcing the Pilot Protocol Python SDK", "slug": "python-sdk-pilot-protocol", "section": "blog", "description": "Native Python bindings for Pilot Protocol. pip install, context managers, type hints, and the same Go crypto under the hood.", "seoTitle": "Announcing the Pilot Protocol Python SDK | Pilot Protocol", "author": "Pilot Protocol editorial team", "publishedAt": "2026-03-19T12:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["python", "sdk"], "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "v1.9.1", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why a Python SDK", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot Protocol's core daemon is written in Go and distributed as static binaries with no runtime dependencies. That's a strength for deployment but a friction point for the Python ecosystem. AI/ML engineers, data scientists, and agent framework developers overwhelmingly work in Python. Asking them to shell out to ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " and parse CLI output is not a real integration.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The Python SDK gives you a native ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Driver", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " class with context managers, type hints, and Pythonic error handling. Under the hood it calls the same Go code through a ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "ctypes", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " FFI layer - same guarantees, no re-implementation.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "a8a23771b12056d119645269", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "pip install pilotprotocol"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "One command installs the SDK, the native ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "libpilot", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " library, and console entry points for ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " and ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilot-daemon", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Python 3.9+, Linux and macOS.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hello World in 8 Lines", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Start the daemon, then:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "fb60e69b5290cc74614749e2", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "python", "code": "from pilotprotocol import Driver\n\nwith Driver() as d:\n    info = d.info()\n    print(f\"I am {info['hostname']} at {info['address']}\")\n\n    peer = d.resolve_hostname(\"other-agent\")[\"address\"]\n    with d.dial(f\"{peer}:1000\") as conn:\n        conn.write(b\"Hello from Python!\")\n        print(conn.read(4096))"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Driver", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " connects to the daemon's Unix socket at ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "/tmp/pilot.sock", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ". The ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "with", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " statement handles cleanup. ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "dial()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " takes a Pilot address and port (", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "N:XXXX.YYYY.YYYY:PORT", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "), so resolve a hostname first; it returns a ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Conn", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " that supports ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "read()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ", ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "write()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "close()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " - exactly what you'd expect from a socket.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "High-Level API: Services Without Boilerplate", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The SDK wraps Pilot's ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "built-in services", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/services", "newTab": false}, "id": "fd82119d09f31e09ee445448"}, {"type": "text", "text": " so you don't have to deal with port numbers or wire formats:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "d7bb79c739ca1191bd8cbb04", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "with Driver() as d:\n    # Data exchange (port 1001)\n    d.send_message(\"peer\", b\"status update\", \"text\")\n    d.send_file(\"peer\", \"/models/weights.bin\")\n\n    # Pub/sub events (port 1002)\n    d.publish_event(\"peer\", \"metrics/gpu\", b\"87.3\")\n    for topic, data in d.subscribe_event(\"peer\", \"metrics/gpu\", timeout=30):\n        print(f\"{topic}: {data}\")"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Topics match exactly, or ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "\"*\"", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " subscribes to every topic on that peer; there are no prefix wildcards.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Each method handles connection setup, framing, and acknowledgment. You send bytes and get dicts back.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Low-Level Streams: Build Your Own Protocol", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "For custom protocols, use ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "dial()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " and ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "listen()", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " directly:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "190c2294098629f0f15c4131", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "python", "code": "from pilotprotocol import Driver\n\n# Server side\nwith Driver() as d:\n    with d.listen(5000) as listener:\n        while True:\n            conn = listener.accept()\n            data = conn.read(4096)\n            conn.write(data)  # Echo\n            conn.close()"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This gives you raw bidirectional streams over Pilot's encrypted tunnels. Every connection gets ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "X25519 + AES-256-GCM encryption", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/blog/zero-dependency-encryption-x25519-aes-gcm", "newTab": false}, "id": "4b6af8a07fa077bb7e408a63"}, {"type": "text", "text": " automatically - no TLS configuration, no certificate management.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Architecture: ctypes FFI to Go", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The SDK doesn't re-implement any protocol logic. It calls into a shared library (", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "libpilot.so", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " / ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "libpilot.dylib", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ") built from the same Go source code that powers the CLI:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "9c949aaafc6bf110853c2d78", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "┌─────────────┐    ctypes/FFI    ┌──────────────┐    Unix socket    ┌────────┐\n│  Python SDK │ ───────────────► │  libpilot.so │ ─────────────────► │ Daemon │\n│  (client.py)│                  │  (Go c-shared)│                   │        │\n└─────────────┘                  └──────────────┘                    └────────┘"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This means:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "list", "children": [{"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Single source of truth", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "- the SDK uses the same Go driver as", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and the same daemon does the encryption and transport for both", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 1}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "No drift", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "- when the Go code gets a bug fix, the Python SDK gets it too (after a wheel rebuild)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 2}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Memory safety", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "- Go's GC manages allocations; the SDK handles cleanup of Go-allocated strings via", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "ctypes", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 3}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Opaque handles", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "- connections and listeners are represented as integer handles, avoiding cross-language pointer issues", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 4}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "listType": "bullet", "start": 1, "tag": "ul"}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Error Handling", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Go errors become Python exceptions:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "a0257f06b157e7b107200489", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "python", "code": "from pilotprotocol import Driver, PilotError\n\nwith Driver() as d:\n    try:\n        conn = d.dial(\"0:0000.0000.9999:1000\", timeout=5)\n    except PilotError as e:\n        print(f\"Failed: {e}\")"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The SDK raises ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "PilotError", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " for protocol-level failures (unreachable peers, trust failures, timeouts), ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "FileNotFoundError", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " when the native library isn't found, and ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "ValueError", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " for invalid parameters. Standard Python exception hierarchy - catch what you need.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Full Type Hints", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every method, parameter, and return value is annotated. Works with mypy, pyright, and IDE autocomplete out of the box:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "952013f803069b415bd8243d", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "python", "code": "from pilotprotocol import Driver, Conn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nwith Driver() as d:\n    conn: Conn = d.dial(\"0:0000.0000.0005:1000\")\n    info: Dict[str, Any] = d.info()"}}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use With Agent Frameworks", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The SDK is designed to integrate with existing Python agent frameworks. A few patterns:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "With LangChain / LangGraph:", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " Use the SDK as a tool - agents can send messages, transfer files, or open streams to trusted peers on the Pilot network as part of their tool chain.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "With ", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "OpenClaw", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/blog/openclaw-meets-pilot-agent-networking-one-command", "newTab": false}, "id": "2d335ecb3d84545ecf41ecd4"}, {"type": "text", "text": ":", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " OpenClaw agents can use the SDK (or ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " directly) to find peers, establish trust, and form ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "multi-agent pipelines", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/blog/multi-agent-pipelines-openclaw-encrypted-tunnels", "newTab": false}, "id": "e48457d4c51be3558f214f56"}, {"type": "text", "text": ".", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "With FastAPI / Flask:", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " Run a local HTTP server that proxies to Pilot peers. Or use the ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "gateway", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/gateway", "newTab": false}, "id": "61b580552333ba9d4f84972a"}, {"type": "text", "text": " to expose Pilot services as local IPs and hit them with standard HTTP clients.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "